  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The five-round granny square adds one more round of clusters to the four-round version, landing at 13 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook after a steam-block. At this size the square is large enough to use as a single-motif front panel for a small cushion cover, or to tile into a blanket grid where you want fewer joins per square metre."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each round adds four new "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "cluster" } }],
            "text": "cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " groups (one per side), so round 5 carries five side clusters per edge. The corner construction stays identical throughout: a (3tr, ch 2, 3tr) pair into each "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "chain-space" } }],
            "text": "chain-space"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on every round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Materials for one motif",
          "body": "About 8 g of DK-weight cotton in one to four colours. A 4 mm crochet hook (UK 8, US G/6). Tapestry needle. Scissors. A blocking mat and pins for the best result."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Gauge" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished five-round granny square measures 13 × 13 cm in DK-weight cotton with a 4 mm hook, after a light steam-block. Make one test motif before starting a large project — tension differences compound across many squares."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Stitches used" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "chain (ch) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "slip stitch (sl st) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "treble (tr) — UK; called double crochet (dc) in US patterns." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "magic ring (MR) — adjustable starting loop; no centre hole." }] }] }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pattern" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked in the round, right side facing throughout. Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first treble of the first cluster. Do not turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 1" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Form a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. *Ch 2, 3 tr into the ring*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 2, sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. Pull tail to close ring. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 2" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st across next 2 tr and into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Into same ch-2 corner sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. *Ch 1, into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr)*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 1, sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 4 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 3" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 8 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 4" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 12 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 5" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] three times. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] three times. Sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. (60 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 16 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chart" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chart reads outward from the magic ring, anti-clockwise. Corner chain-2 spaces mark the four corners; chain-1 spaces appear between clusters along the sides."
          }
        ]
      },
