        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The five-round square joins at its four corner ch-2 spaces and its 16 side ch-1 spaces. For a blanket grid, whip-stitch through the back loops with a tapestry needle, or use a flat slip-stitch join with RS together. At 13 cm per square, a 5 x 7 grid gives approximately 65 x 91 cm — a generous lap blanket from 35 squares."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Care" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handwash in cool water with a small amount of mild soap, or machine-wash on a wool/delicates cycle. Do not tumble-dry. Lay flat on a clean towel and ease to shape while damp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "What to try next" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The six-round version adds one more edge cluster per side and lands at 15 cm, the standard cushion-cover panel size. For colour contrast without changing the structure, try the two-colour or three-colour granny square — the same five rounds but with yarn changes between rounds."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
